  <reporting-org ref="XI-IATI-EC_INTPA" secondary-reporter="0" type="15">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">European Commission - Directorate-General for International Partnerships</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Accelerating the energy transition in Namibia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In line with the Namibia Multiannual Indicative Plan 2021-2027, priority area 2, Inclusive Green Growth, the action will contribute to the Specific Objective 2.1 of the MIP: An increased share of renewable energies in the energy mix will facilitate a stronger and greener economic recovery. The action will also support the achievement of Goal 3 of the Harambee Prosperity Plan II &#xbf; Developing Complementary Engines of Growth&#xbf;, with specific focus on Activities 1 and 2 which aims at projecting Namibia to become a sub- Saharan powerhouse for renewable energy generation and a frontrunner in the green hydrogen and synthetic fuels new market.The above political objectives will be supported through the achievement of the Specific Objectives of the Action, which are:1.To increase sustainable energy generation and access2.To support development of green hydrogen and synthetic fuels value chainTo equip formal and informal Namibian workers, including women and youth, with the relevant skills and qualifications necessary to participate in the green hydrogen and renewable energy industries.</narrative>
  </description>
